{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Complementary)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Complementary)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Azar and Carl play a game of tic-tac-toe. Azar places an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> one of the boxes in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-by-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> array of boxes, then Carl places an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in one of the remaining boxes. After that, Azar places an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in one of the remaining boxes, and so on until all 9 boxes are filled or one of the players has 3 of their symbols in a row—horizontal, vertical, or diagonal—whichever comes first, in which case that player wins the game. Suppose the players make their moves at random, rather than trying to follow a rational strategy, and that Carl wins the game when he places his third <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. How many ways can the board look after the game is over?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd504acce7a0b02be8a2780741abc4a8ff6e24f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 36 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 112 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 120 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 148 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"437\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need to find out the number of configurations with 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in a row, and 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> not in a row.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9154c3cf3af5df5469bbb7b40718758979f2bb95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 1}$\" width=\"54\" height=\"11\" />: 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are in a horizontal row or a vertical row.\n</p><p>Step 1: We determine the row that 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> occupy.\n</p><p>The number of ways is 6.\n</p><p>Step 2: We determine the configuration of 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The number of ways is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d928bb7f7d9cd3974a18578fb5f7ef950f8c786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{3} - 2 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"113\" height=\"55\" />. (6 open spots to put the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and subtracting cases where they fill row/column)\n</p><p>In this case, following from the rule of product, the number of ways is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/a/d2a6b81c1ab3fbb5514ba97b1022966f852152e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 18 = 108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901dd3d64f25ed84522adca7c7693a46693cbcf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 2}$\" width=\"54\" height=\"11\" />: 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are in a diagonal row.\n</p><p>Step 1: We determine the row that 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> occupy.\n</p><p>The number of ways is 2.\n</p><p>Step 2: We determine the configuration of 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The number of ways is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4103126cd01d67e024c33d1752e5318b0273cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{3}  = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, following from the rule of product, the number of ways is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/55617fe9664889666d760624f46b4251c8949fd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 20 = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Putting all cases together, the total number of ways is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19aeff50ab6a014e8ad9336c40c26da7856f759e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108 + 40 = 148$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4911cab8bbfcf54129ad7ade12dd837c238258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }148}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Complementary.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Complementary)\">Solution 2 (Complementary)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Complementary)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First count all the ways to have 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in a row and 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can be arranged in 8 possible ways (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> horizontal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> vertical, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> diagonal), and in each case, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> can be arranged in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/75569481af3db5bdcc1959c92cc955928d9c25ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> ways, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/7246de4add406141bc7bf80bfdff84d394d2ad2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8* \\binom{6}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"65\" height=\"55\" /> = 160 arrangements.\n</p><p>Now exclude the ones in which the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are also in a row column. Either the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> both form rows, which can be achieved in 6 ways, or they both form columns, which can also be acheived in 6 ways. Excluding these 12 arrangements, the answer is shown to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4911cab8bbfcf54129ad7ade12dd837c238258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }148}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kxgUdv_L-ys?t=796\">https://youtu.be/kxgUdv_L-ys?t=796</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity\">Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OpRk-iposj8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OpRk-iposj8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solved Mentally writing only the answer, and then regular way also\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DE3P50S7EWw?si=HPY5cYrcZfcBpe4C\">https://youtu.be/DE3P50S7EWw?si=HPY5cYrcZfcBpe4C</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A\">2021 Fall AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017153717\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 298/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2448/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 308/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6910/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.429      1 -total\n 62.38%    8.377      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 36.06%    4.843      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22236:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017153717 and revision id 268801. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}